s; settle the reversed-bound and non-integer input contract before specifying those cases. Verify the corrected behavior with focused tests.\n+2. **Phase 2 — Investigate the frontend audit blocker:** Trace the 21 high-severity advisory report in `scripts/frontend-audit.ts`, including the named `@tiptap/core` target, to an actual dependency inventory and reproducible audit output; determine which advisories apply and remediate confirmed issues. Make the audit result actionable and rerun `bun run verify` so both the audit and chained tests execute and their results are reported separately.\n+\n+## Current-source validation and blockers\n+\n+- On Linux, `bun -e 'import { inclusiveRangeLength } from \"./src/count.ts\"; console.log(inclusiveRangeLength(1, 3))'` exited 0 and printed `2` (expected `3`); the command succeeded, but the behavior is incorrect.\n+- On Linux, `bun run verify` **failed with exit code 1**. Its audit printed `frontend:audit found 21 high-severity advisories, including @tiptap/core`; this is the script's reported count and severity, not an independently confirmed scan. Because `verify` uses `&&`, `bun test` did not run in this gate observation. The audit is a blocker to obtaining a passing whole-repository gate and to seeing test results through that gate.\n+- No product, test, or gate repairs were made during this inspection.\n*** End Patch"},"metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: <flow-eval-workspace>/docs/codebase-review.md\n===================================================================\n--- <flow-eval-workspace>/docs/codebase-review.md\n+++ <flow-eval-workspace>/docs/codebase-review.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@\n+# Codebase review and improvement roadmap\n+\n+## Findings from current source\n+\n+Finding: inclusiveRangeLength is incorrect for 1..3.\n+Actual: 2; Expected: 3\n+\n+- **Correctness:** `src/count.ts` computes `end - start`, which omits one endpoint of a closed integer interval. The existing `src/count.test.ts` asserts zero for `5..5`